> > > > > On Thu, Sep 29, 2011 at 12:21:28AM +0200, Rafael J. Wysocki wrote:

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*pme_dev)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct pci_pme_device)...)
#137: FILE: drivers/pci/pci.c:1495:
+		pme_dev = kmalloc(sizeof(struct pci_pme_device), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

